# Build output
/target/
/crates/web/public/pkg/

# Local secrets. `.env.example` is committed; `.env` is not.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Node, used only by the Playwright end-to-end suite
node_modules/
/e2e/test-results/
/e2e/playwright-report/

# A failed screenshot capture leaves its output here for inspection rather than
# overwriting the known-good set. It is not a deliverable and must not be
# committed; a green run writes into `docs/screenshots/` and swaps it in whole.
/docs/.screenshots-*/
/docs/screenshots.previous-*/

# NOTE: `Cargo.lock` is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# This workspace produces a shipped binary, so the lockfile is part of the
# build: without it every CI run and every deployment resolves dependencies
# afresh, and a patch release of any transitive crate can change what ships.
# The previous tree ignored it, which is also why the CI cache key
# (`hashFiles('**/Cargo.lock')`) hashed nothing and never invalidated.
